.TH SDL_HINT_MAC_PRESS_AND_HOLD 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_MAC_PRESS_AND_HOLD \- A variable controlling whether holding down a key will repeat the pressed key or open the accents menu on macOS.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_MAC_PRESS_AND_HOLD \(dqSDL_MAC_PRESS_AND_HOLD\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Holding a key will repeat the pressed key\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Holding a key will open the accents menu for that key\[char46] (default)
.PP
This hint needs to be set before
.BR SDL_Init ()\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

